## Answer

[RUN] All 21 declared route–learning-rate cells were run and all remained
finite through 500 epochs. None passed the convergence rule fixed before the
sweep: stability from epoch 400 to 500 of the training objective, held-out
level R², held-out within-group ordering, and held-out top-1. There is therefore
no learning-rate selection to make. In particular, none of the three current
literals is admissible.

[INFERRED] Under the fixed selection rule, the finding is that 500 epochs is
the wrong horizon for each of these architectures on these panels. This does
not imply that every rate would fail at a longer horizon, and the run does not
pick the rate with the best predictive result at epoch 500.

**Loss values below are convergence diagnostics only and are never evidence
about EE. No EE quantity was computed, so no EE result could influence this
finding.** No production training, policy run, or acceptance test was run.

## Rule fixed before running

[DERIVED] For objective `L`, objective stability means
`abs(L500-L400) / max(abs(L400), 1e-12) <= 0.01`. Predictive stability means
absolute 400-to-500 changes no larger than `0.01` for level R² and `0.005` for
each of ordering and top-1. A cell is admissible exactly when it stays finite
through 500 and all four checks pass. This formula, the grid, and the data
boundaries were written before the full process started in
`.scratch/lr-convergence-sweep/spec.md`.

“Last material improvement” is the destination epoch of the last adjacent
sampled interval, including 0→100, in which loss decreased by more than 1%
relative or the named held-out metric increased by more than its absolute
tolerance. `—` means no sampled interval did so. “Stable L/R/O/T” reports the
four 400→500 tests in order: loss, R², ordering, top-1. A material decline also
fails stability even though it is not an improvement.

## Schemas and panels

[RUN] C1 used the repaired `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2`, digest
`66ed4a3f9222ac7f20f4334ffab92f6164d2dad203cbac7f7d4e1728ae4ad654`,
on the same coherent 37-anchor prefix as C1REALV2: 36,360 rows and 3,700
`(anchor,user)` groups.

[RUN] C2 used `mcrl-v025-stagec-q2-action-v1`, digest
`a891dd9831d76bccd981cef054ff204fa1d49c3cf6e5f3265015f16f1057019c`,
on the same 20 anchors as C2REAL: 19,647 rows and 2,000 groups. A repaired Q2
schema is not reachable: Q1 v2 changes only `q1_state`, while C2 consumes the
22-slot `q2_state`; the public Q1-v2 projection has already verified that this
field is copied exactly. Thus C2 is explicitly the requested v1 fallback, not
a silently relabelled v2 result.

[RUN] C3 used the available repaired-v2 joint route state on the twelve
completed two-world exact anchors (steps 0–5) frozen before this sweep: 11,947
catalogue rows, of which 2,541 size≥2 rows train the head. The size counts are
`{0: 12, 1: 9,394, 2: 2,331, 3: 93, 4: 47, 5: 40, 6: 1, 7: 2, 8: 3,
100: 24}`. Hence 78.63% of evaluation rows are singletons and 21.27% are
trainable nontrivial coalitions. Direct inspection of all twelve frozen NPZ
inputs found exact zero Psi on all 9,394 singleton rows. The one completed
per-process generator receipt available at validation time (world 1, step 0)
reported maximum decomposition residual `8.882e-15`; the remaining live
generator ranges had not yet emitted their process-level receipts, so no
all-anchor decomposition claim is made here.

[DERIVED] C3 singleton targets must be zero because
`Psi_{i} = Delta F({i}) - d_i`, while `d_i` is that same unilateral increment.
The full-support C3 R² values are therefore strongly aided by structurally easy
zeros; they should not be read as evidence of a well-fitted interaction head.

All LOAO fits used the first sealed pilot seed
`V025_LEARNER/seed/1` (`6407676579069309528`), the literal sealed architectures
and optimizer fields, and one deterministic full-batch Adam update per epoch.
Only the learning-rate field passed to `AdamMLPHead.create` changed. C1/C2 used
the same deterministic 4,096-pair cap as C1REAL/C2REAL. C3 aggregated all
training-anchor gradients into one full-batch update per epoch and hard-set
empty/singleton predictions to zero.

[RUN] The common-initialization parameter L2 norms were `4.4561` (C1),
`19.9039` (C2), and `16.0125` (C3). The epoch-500 tables give fold means and
ranges against those baselines, making near-initial, growing, and large-scale
fits distinguishable.

